# Migrations are checksummed, so their bytes are part of the contract.
#
# `sqlx::migrate!` embeds each file at COMPILE time and stores a checksum in
# `_sqlx_migrations` when it is applied; on every later start it re-checks that
# sum and refuses to run if it moved ("migration N was previously applied but
# has been modified"). Line endings are content as far as that checksum is
# concerned, so a file that is LF in the repository and CRLF in a Windows
# working copy produces two different sums for the same migration — a binary
# built on Windows then refuses to start against a database migrated by a
# Linux build, and vice versa. Pinning them to LF everywhere removes the
# discrepancy at the source.
*.sql text eol=lf

# The `.sqlx` query cache is generated and compared byte-for-byte by
# `cargo sqlx prepare --check` in CI; same reasoning.
*.json text eol=lf
